  "textContent": "Filming for the television special James Paul McCartney continued on 19 March 1973 at Elstree Studios. Produced by ATV, James Paul McCartney was first broadcast on 16 April 1973 in the USA, and 10 May in the UK. It was released on DVD as part of the super deluxe reissue of in Red Rose Speedway December 2018.\n\n\n\n\n\nPage last updated: 28 November 2025Also on this day...1999: Ringo Starr and his All-Starr Band live: Silver Legacy, Reno1979: Recording: Getting Closer by Wings1975: Mixing: Rock Show, Love In Song, You Gave Me The Answer, Magneto And Titanium Man, Letting Go by Wings1972: Mixing: Angela, The Luck Of The Irish, New York City by John Lennon and Yoko Ono1971: John Lennon, George Harrison and Ringo Starr file appeal against High Court ruling1965: Filming: Help!, Austria1964: The Beatles’ first Top Of The Pops appearance1964: The Beatles are given Variety Club awards1964: Filming: A Hard Day’s Night1963: The Beatles live: Regal Cinema, Cambridge1962: The Beatles live: Kingsway Club, Southport1961: The Beatles live: Casbah Coffee Club, LiverpoolWant more? Visit the Beatles history section.",
